window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0e09d3699dec6a33"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-an-onboarding-portal\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">入职引导门户</h1> <p>帮助新员工找到下一项任务，并练习即将承担的工作。</p> <p>将团队的第一周计划转化为每日活动、资源链接和练习任务，并保存进度，让每位新员工都能从上次离开的地方继续。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>为多名新员工安排同一岗位入职流程的经理。</li> <li>负责维护新员工第一周计划和资源的人力资源团队（People team）。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建入职引导门户</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 @Sites，根据我们的第一周计划为[role or team]（岗位或团队）构建一个入职引导门户。本周结束时的目标是[for example, draft a customer kickoff agenda]（例如：起草客户启动会议议程）。\n\n资料来源：\n- 第一周计划：[attached file or document link]（附件或文档链接）。\n- 产品和团队资源：[specific document or folder links]（具体文档或文件夹链接）。\n- 练习任务说明和示例：[links]（链接）。\n- 联系人及其职责：[supplied list]（提供的名单）。\n\n先确认你能读取哪些资料。按日期列出任务，并附上来源链接、说明和联系人。对缺失或相互矛盾的信息提出问题；不要编造任务、人员或公司政策。\n\n构建欢迎页面、每日检查清单、资源列表、帮助联系人，以及周末练习任务。对每项任务说明要做什么、为什么重要、完成后是什么样子、对应的资源链接，以及可以向谁求助。只有计划中提供了预计时长时，才显示时长。将练习任务链接到其说明、已批准示例和评审标准。遵循所提供计划中的顺序。添加进度条和“从上次进度继续”部分。将完成状态视为活动记录，而不是对工作准备程度的评分。\n\n要求用户登录，并在访问之间保存每个人的任务完成情况。将进度设为仅本人可见，并在服务器端强制执行记录访问权限。将共享的任务内容与个人进度分开。为任务分配稳定标识，避免说明或链接更新时清除已有完成记录。\n\n使用经过审核的计划副本，并保留指向原始资源的链接。说明源文档更改后需要更新网站。不要把受限资源的内容复制到面向更广受众的页面中，也不要将完成数据写回源文档。如果无法读取某个来源，请索取可访问的副本或链接。\n\n测试新用户、部分完成的进度、已完成的计划和第二个账户。确认进度在重新加载后仍会保留、保持私密，而且不会因修改说明而重置。标出仍需新员工检查访问权限的资源链接。将网站设为仅对我们的工作区开放。发布之前，先展示已保存的预览、测试结果和待确认问题。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-56e8c36f028eb49f?anchor=save-records-and-progress\">保存记录和进度</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e0f092cc982945c2?anchor=add-sign-in-with-chatgpt\">添加 Sign in with ChatGPT</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">开始之前</h2> <p>把第一周计划变成一个新员工可以查看今天要做什么、查找合适资源，并从上次进度继续的地方。你可以要求创建一个门户，将每日任务、帮助联系人和周末练习任务汇集在一起，并为每个人保存进度。</p> <p>先选择一个岗位，并明确写出新员工到本周结束时应该能够完成什么。这个目标有助于你决定计划中应包括哪些资源和活动。收集团队已经在使用的材料：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>资料来源</th> <th>示例</th> <th>可提供的内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>第一周计划</td> <td>包含日期、任务、说明、资源和联系人的文档或电子表格</td> <td>每日检查清单</td> </tr> <tr> <td>团队资源</td> <td>产品概览、团队目录和岗位专用模板</td> <td>每项任务的链接和背景信息</td> </tr> <tr> <td>练习任务</td> <td>说明、评审标准和已批准的示例</td> <td>清晰的周末目标</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>把任务写得足够具体，让人能判断何时完成。例如，“了解产品”可以具体写成“阅读产品概览，并在与入职伙伴的交流会上提出两个问题”。如果计划提供了预计时长，请将其列出；还要说明哪些活动需要他人协助。</p> <p><a id=\"example-preparing-for-a-customer-kickoff\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">示例：准备客户启动会议</h3> <p>在这个假设性的客户成功经理计划中，本周的活动逐步引导新员工起草一份启动会议议程：</p> <ul> <li><strong>熟悉情况：</strong> 阅读产品概览，并与入职伙伴会面讨论问题。</li> <li><strong>了解实际工作：</strong> 观看一个已批准的启动会议示例，并记下主持人提出的问题。</li> <li><strong>尝试完成任务：</strong> 使用团队模板起草议程，然后与经理讨论。</li> </ul> <p>对于其他岗位，可以替换为相关任务，例如准备营销活动简报，或处理模拟的支持请求。请使用经过批准的计划来确定具体活动和顺序。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-your-sources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">连接资料来源</h2> <ol> <li>在构建对话中附上入职计划。对于位于已连接应用中的文档，请先询问 ChatGPT 当前可以使用哪些连接，然后提供准确的计划、资源或文件夹链接，并完成它要求的连接步骤。举例来说，如果相应连接可用，可以指向 Google Drive 或 SharePoint 中的“客户成功：第一周”和“启动会议议程模板”。请点明具体文件，不要让它搜索公司里的所有文档。</li> <li>让 ChatGPT 按日期列出找到的任务，并为每项任务附上来源链接和联系人。在构建网站之前先补齐遗漏内容。文档链接只能指出资料来源；如果需要使用文档内容，请确认 ChatGPT 能够读取它。</li> <li>在网站中使用经过审核的计划副本，并保留指向原始资源的链接。之后对源文档的修改不会自动同步到副本。要修订计划，请在构建对话中提供更新后的来源。</li> <li>如果你希望访客访问网站时从已连接的应用加载资源，请单独提出请求。使用仅限工作区访问的网站，并使用新员工本人的应用权限进行测试。有关连接流程，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites/data-and-connections#build-a-site-with-connected-data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">数据与连接</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites/data-and-connections\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。</li> </ol> <p>请与一名拥有和新员工相同访问权限的同事一起打开资源链接。在分享网站前，先修复无法访问的材料。个人完成记录保存在网站中即可，不需要写回入职文档。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use-it\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li>先显示下一步操作</li> </ol> <p>使用起始提示词，并附上计划和资源链接。以刚入职员工的视角检查第一天的安排：他们应该知道从哪项任务开始、任务为何重要、应打开什么，以及可以向谁求助。请 ChatGPT 将模糊的任务标签替换为计划中的具体操作，并把相关资源放在每项任务旁边。</p> <ol> <li>逐步完成练习任务</li> </ol> <p>按照整周活动逐步完成练习任务。新员工应能找到任务说明、已批准的示例，以及经理会检查的内容。以启动会议计划为例，可以检查议程是否说明会议目的、包含面向客户的问题，并留出商定后续步骤的时间。</p> <p>将一项活动标记为完成，重新加载页面，并在另一个会话中返回，检查进度是否已保存。使用第二个账户验证它会显示自己的进度，并且无法访问第一个人的记录。已完成的检查清单只记录活动；如果要了解此人还需要哪些帮助，请结合练习任务和沟通来判断。</p> <ol> <li>欢迎下一位新员工</li> </ol> <p>检查网站的受众设置，并为团队发布网站。在欢迎信息中附上链接，并说明新员工每天如何使用该网站。在周末沟通时，询问哪些说明或资源难以理解。计划有变时，请 ChatGPT 在发布更新前保留已完成的任务，并说明新增或移除的任务会如何影响进度。</p> <p><a id=\"take-it-further\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">进一步优化</h2> <p><a id=\"refresh-the-plan-from-its-source\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">根据源计划更新内容</h3> <p>入职计划更改时更新检查清单，同时保留已完成的任务，并明确说明这些更改对现有进度的影响。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Read the updated onboarding plan at [document link or attached file]. Compare it with the site's current tasks and show additions, removals, and changed instructions. Keep existing task identities and saved completion records wherever the task is the same. Ask me how to handle removed or substantially changed tasks. Update only the reviewed plan and resource links, then show a preview before publishing.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">阅读 [document link or attached file] 中更新后的入职计划。将它与网站当前的任务比较，展示新增、删除和指令变更。只要任务仍是同一项，就保留其现有任务标识和已保存的完成记录。对于被删除或发生重大变化的任务，询问我应如何处理。只更新已经审阅的计划及资源链接，然后在发布前展示预览。</div></div> <p><a id=\"put-the-next-task-first\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">优先显示下一项任务</h3> <p>帮助每位新员工继续处理第一项未完成的任务，同时不要隐藏本周的其他计划。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add a Continue where you left off section showing the signed-in person's first unfinished task, its day, instructions, resource link, and contact. Keep the full week available. Show a completion message when all tasks are done. Test a new user, a partially completed plan, and a completed plan, and confirm that each person's saved progress remains private.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">添加一个“继续上次进度”区域，显示当前登录者的第一项未完成任务、所属日期、说明、资源链接和联系人。仍然保留整周的完整内容。所有任务完成时显示完成提示。测试新用户、部分完成的计划以及全部完成的计划，并确认每个人已保存的进度仍然私密。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-an-onboarding-portal\">Build an onboarding portal</h1> <p>Help new hires find their next task and practice the work they'll be doing.</p> <p>Turn your team's first-week plan into daily activities, resource links, and a practice task, with saved progress so each new hire can pick up where they left off.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Managers onboarding several people into the same role.</li> <li>People teams maintaining first-week plans and resources for new hires.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build an onboarding portal</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @Sites to build an onboarding portal for [role or team] from our first-week plan. The end-of-week goal is [for example, draft a customer kickoff agenda].\n\nSources:\n- First-week plan: [attached file or document link].\n- Product and team resources: [specific document or folder links].\n- Practice-task instructions and example: [links].\n- Contacts and their responsibilities: [supplied list].\n\nFirst confirm which sources you can read. List the tasks by day with their source links, instructions, and contacts. Ask about missing or conflicting details; don't invent tasks, people, or company policies.\n\nBuild a welcome page, a day-by-day checklist, a resource list, helpful contacts, and the end-of-week practice task. For each task, show what to do, why it matters, what a completed task looks like, its resource link, and who can help. Include estimated times only where the plan provides them. Link the practice task to its instructions, approved example, and review criteria. Use the sequence in the supplied plan. Add a progress bar and a Continue where you left off section. Treat completion as a record of activities, not a score of job readiness.\n\nRequire sign-in and save each person's task completion between visits. Keep progress private to that person and enforce record access on the server. Keep shared task content separate from individual progress. Give tasks stable identities so an instruction or link update doesn't erase completion records.\n\nUse a reviewed copy of the plan and links to original resources. Explain that source-document changes need a site update. Don't copy restricted resource contents into a page for a broader audience or write completion data back into source documents. If a source can't be read, ask for an accessible copy or link.\n\nTest a new user, partial progress, a completed plan, and a second account. Confirm that progress survives reload, remains private, and isn't reset by an instruction edit. Flag resource links that still need a new hire's access check. Keep the site private to our workspace. Show a saved preview, test results, and open questions before publishing.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-56e8c36f028eb49f?anchor=save-records-and-progress\">Save records and progress</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e0f092cc982945c2?anchor=add-sign-in-with-chatgpt\">Add Sign in with ChatGPT</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Turn your first-week plan into a place where new hires can see what to do today, find the right resources, and pick up where they left off. Ask for a portal that brings daily tasks, helpful contacts, and an end-of-week practice task together, with progress saved for each person.</p> <p>Choose a role and name something a new hire should be able to do by the end of the week. That goal helps you decide which resources and activities belong in the plan. Gather the materials your team already uses:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Source</th> <th>Example</th> <th>What it contributes</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>First-week plan</td> <td>A document or spreadsheet with day, task, instructions, resource, and contact</td> <td>The daily checklist</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Team resources</td> <td>A product overview, team directory, and role-specific templates</td> <td>Links and context for each task</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Practice task</td> <td>Instructions, review criteria, and an approved example</td> <td>A clear goal for the end of the week</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Make tasks concrete enough that someone can tell when they're done. “Learn the product” could become “Read the product overview and bring two questions to your buddy meeting.” Include an estimated time if your plan provides one, and explain which activities need another person's help.</p> <h3 id=\"example-preparing-for-a-customer-kickoff\">Example: Preparing for a customer kickoff</h3> <p>In this hypothetical plan for a customer success manager, the week's activities build toward drafting a kickoff agenda:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Get oriented:</strong> Read the product overview and meet a buddy to discuss questions.</li> <li><strong>See the work:</strong> Watch an approved sample kickoff and note the questions the host asks.</li> <li><strong>Try the task:</strong> Draft an agenda using the team's template, then discuss it with a manager.</li> </ul> <p>For another role, substitute a relevant task, such as preparing a campaign brief or handling a sample support request. Use your approved plan to set the activities and sequence.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-your-sources\">Connect your sources</h2> <ol> <li>Attach the onboarding plan in the build conversation. For documents in a connected app, ask ChatGPT which connections are available, then give it the exact plan, resource, or folder links. Complete any connection step it requests. For example, point to “Customer success: first week” and “Kickoff agenda template” in Google Drive or SharePoint, if the relevant connection is available. Name the exact files instead of asking it to search all company documents.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to list the tasks it found, grouped by day, with the source link and contact for each. Correct gaps before it builds the site. A document link identifies a source; confirm that ChatGPT can read it when you need its contents.</li> <li>Use the plan as a reviewed copy in the site and keep links to original resources. A later edit to the source document won't automatically update that copy. To revise the plan, return to the build conversation with the updated source.</li> <li>If resources should load from a connected app when someone visits, request that separately. Use a workspace-private site, and test with the new hire's own app permissions. Follow <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites/data-and-connections#build-a-site-with-connected-data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">data and connections</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites/data-and-connections\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a> for the connection flow.</li> </ol> <p>Open the resource links with a colleague who has the same access as a new hire. Fix inaccessible materials before sharing the site. Keep individual completion records in the site; they don't need to be written back into the onboarding document.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use-it\">How to use it</h2> <ol> <li>Put the next action first</li> </ol> <p>Use the starter prompt with your plan and resource links. Review the first day as someone who has just joined. They should know which task to start, why it matters, what to open, and who can help. Ask ChatGPT to replace vague task labels with actions from the plan and put the relevant resource beside each task.</p> <ol> <li>Work toward the practice task</li> </ol> <p>Follow the week's activities through to the practice task. The new hire should be able to find the instructions, an approved example, and what their manager will look for. In the sample kickoff plan, that might mean checking that the agenda states the meeting's purpose, includes questions for the customer, and leaves time to agree on next steps.</p> <p>Mark an activity complete, reload, and return in another session to check that progress is saved. Use a second account to verify that it starts with its own progress and can't access the first person's record. A completed checklist records activities; use the practice task and conversation to understand where the person still needs help.</p> <ol> <li>Welcome the next hire</li> </ol> <p>Review the audience and publish the site for your team. Include its link in your welcome message, and explain how the new hire can use it each day. Ask which instructions or resources were hard to follow during the end-of-week conversation. When the plan changes, ask ChatGPT to preserve completed tasks and explain how new or removed tasks affect progress before publishing the update.</p> <h2 id=\"take-it-further\">Take it further</h2> <h3 id=\"refresh-the-plan-from-its-source\">Refresh the plan from its source</h3> <p>Update the checklist when the onboarding plan changes, while preserving completed tasks and making changes to existing progress explicit.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Read the updated onboarding plan at [document link or attached file]. Compare it with the site's current tasks and show additions, removals, and changed instructions. Keep existing task identities and saved completion records wherever the task is the same. Ask me how to handle removed or substantially changed tasks. Update only the reviewed plan and resource links, then show a preview before publishing.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"put-the-next-task-first\">Put the next task first</h3> <p>Help each new hire resume their first unfinished task without hiding the rest of the week's plan.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add a Continue where you left off section showing the signed-in person's first unfinished task, its day, instructions, resource link, and contact. Keep the full week available. Show a completion message when all tasks are done. Test a new user, a partially completed plan, and a completed plan, and confirm that each person's saved progress remains private.\n</code></pre>"};
